Hello! This PR allows mods to specify an Initialization method that is run when the mod DLL is loaded. Here's an example of code that would be in a mod:

```cs
public static partial class Patches {
	public static void Initialize() {
		Logger.Info("Applying patches");

		Harmony harmony = new Harmony("amsam0.MoSimMod");
		harmony.PatchAll(typeof(Patches));

		Logger.Info("Initialized!");
	}
}
```

The idea is to allow for HarmonyX patches to be included in mods. It would be better to bundle HarmonyX with MoSim and use `harmony.PatchAll(assembly)` when loading the assembly, but I thought I'd propose this somewhat naive alternative to do it before investing time to add full HarmonyX support. Neither methods are better in terms of security - both would allow for arbitrary code execution when a mod is loaded (which is already possible).
